Movement edit:
```
const forward = input.forward || 0;
const strafe = input.strafe || 0;
let wishX = 0, wishZ = 0;
if (forward || strafe) {
 const len=Math.hypot...
 const f=forward/len; s=...
 ...
}
const wantsSprint = ...
const speed = wantsSprint ? 9.6 : 5.5;
...
this.vel.x = damp(..., wishX * speed, ...)
```
We need retain magnitude. Add `const wishMag = Math.min(1, Math.hypot(forward, strafe));` outside. Then speed multiplier.

```
const speed = (wantsSprint ? 9.6 : 5.5) * (wishMag > 0 ? Math.min(1, wishMag) : 0);
```
But keyboard diagonal wishMag min(1,1.414)=1. Good. If controller barely moves 0.2, speed 1.1 m/s. Fine. But applying to wishX*0.2 after normalization yields desired. Actually wishX is normalized direction *1; multiply by speed*wishMag. Good. But sprint wants forward > 0.1 and stamina; if analog full, speed 9.6. Good.

But if touch input analog values maybe 0.9, fine.

Also jump indexing. Fine.

